      "side": 0,
      "message": "The aim for the change was to fix automotive use cases where external displays should be auto-enabled on user builds and the original ENABLE_ON_CONNECT sysprop check was gated behind Build.IS_ENG || Build.IS_USERDEBUG, making it ineffective in production. \n\nI agree the existing logic should be preserved. Can we go with the following approach:                                                                                              \n   \n  private boolean shouldAutoEnable(LogicalDisplay logicalDisplay) {                                                                                                                                                \n      if (SystemProperties.getBoolean(ENABLE_ON_CONNECT, false)) return true;                                                                                                                                      \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \n      // If using the new connection dialog, don\u0027t auto enable so the dialog                                                                                                                                       \n      // has a reason to show                                                                                                                                                                                      \n      if (mFlags.isUpdatedDisplayConnectionDialogEnabled()) return false;                                                                                                                                          \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \n      if (mLogicalDisplayMapper.isEnabledInLayoutLocked(logicalDisplay)) return true;                                                                                                                              \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \n      return mFlags.isDisplayContentModeManagementEnabled()                                                                                                                                                        \n              \u0026\u0026 logicalDisplay.canHostTasksLocked();                                                                                                                                                              \n  } \n  \n This preserves the dialog and content mode management paths.",
      "parentUuid": "9e13751d_d68e2c0b",
      "revId": "45034f0663f960d9ee5fb0a101a4732b71f6e2f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
